  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "kind": "prep",
      "primary_message": "Roughly chop the escarole. Finely slice the onion. Finely chop the celery. Peel and dice the carrot into 1/2-inch pieces. Thinly slice the garlic. Cut the very cold boneless skinless chicken breast half into 1-inch chunks.",
      "secondary_message": "1 head escarole\n1 medium onion\n1 medium stalk celery\n1 medium carrot\n3 cloves garlic\n1 very cold boneless skinless chicken breast half, about 8 ounces"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "primary_message": "Heat olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat until shimmering. Add escarole, onion, celery, carrot, and garlic and cook, stirring frequently, until vegetables are softened but not browned, about 15 minutes. Add chicken stock, bay leaf, and Parmesan rind. Bring to a boil, reduce to a bare simmer, and cook until vegetables are fully softened and flavors are developed, about 45 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, combine chicken, cheese, heavy cream egg, nutmeg, and 1 teaspoon kosher salt (or 1/2 teaspoon table salt) in a large bowl. Season well with black pepper. Toss with hands to combine. Transfer mixture to a food processor and process until smooth, about 30 seconds. Transfer to a piping bag fitted with a 1.5-cm round tip, or to a heavy duty zipper-lock bag with a 1.5-cm hole cut in one corner.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "primary_message": "When soup is cooked, make the meatballs by piping them over the hot soup, cutting them off in 1.5-cm segments with the tip of a sharp paring knife. When all the dumplings are used, bring soup to a boil and simmer for 5 minutes. Discard bay leaf and Parmesan rind, season to taste with salt and pepper, stir in parsley, and serve, drizzling with more extra-virgin olive oil at the table.",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
